/-!
# The corrected smooth renormalised model

Exports explicit tree functions, genuine Q-distributions and the abstract
Model fields on the entire retained type, the exact source-induced positive
character, full H0 tensor agreement, causal admissibility and full compact
Pi/Gamma bounds, hence finite compact model norms. These are the existence
ingredients of the renormalised canonical model on the retained type;
uniqueness is proved separately from weighted Π/Γ bounds.

Sources: Hairer [Hai14, (8.34), (9.3)–(9.5), Theorem 8.44].
-/

